@inject IStringLocalizer<ClientCopy> Localizer

@*
    The application shell.

    Superseded 2026-08-29 by story 1.3. This previously said the shell "deliberately does not use
    <Router>: there are no routable pages yet, and a Router with an empty route table cannot
    resolve its NotFound case" - which described story 1.1's tree and stopped being true when
    Pages/Register.razor landed. It also carried a paragraph recording what its story-1.1 comment
    had said before story 1.2 corrected it.

    That accumulation is itself a recorded finding - deferred-work.md:44 notes that review
    archaeology is piling up in these files and assigns the convention decision to Lee, once, for
    the project. This story does not act on it (it is not the next story's to take), but it does
    not add a third layer either: the superseded story-1.1 paragraph is gone, and what is left is
    one line saying what changed and why.

    FocusOnNavigate moves focus to the routed page's <h1> after every navigation. Without it a
    single-page application changes the whole document under a screen-reader user while their
    focus stays wherever the last link was - which is the most common accessibility defect in
    client-side routing, and registration is named first among NFR-9's five gated flows.
*@

<Router AppAssembly="@typeof(App).Assembly">
    <Found Context="routeData">
        <RouteView RouteData="@routeData" DefaultLayout="@typeof(MainLayout)" />
        <FocusOnNavigate RouteData="@routeData" Selector="h1" />
    </Found>
    <NotFound>
        <LayoutView Layout="@typeof(MainLayout)">
            <div class="auth-surface">
                <div class="auth-panel">
                    <h1 class="type-dialog-title auth-panel__heading">@Localizer["NotFoundHeading"]</h1>
                    <p class="auth-panel__intro">@Localizer["NotFoundBody"]</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </LayoutView>
    </NotFound>
</Router>
